HOW TO FIND OUT ABOUT ANYTHING ON THIS DISK===========================================    man <name>It shows everything the disk has about a program: its manual page, thenits other documents, one after another.  A program with no documentsgets a page saying what it is and what it answers when asked for help.    man -k <word>     which programs are about <word>    man -f <name>     what a program is, in one line    man -w <name>     where its documents and source are    man -s <name>     read its source    man               this listReading: space pages on, b back, /word searches, :n next document, :pthe one before, q leaves.Behind it are two files, generated from the disk by tools/gen_docmap.py:    DOC/WHATIS   one line for every program    DOC/DOCS     each program's documents and source, a path to a lineA program cannot be missing from them, and they name no file that isnot here.OTHER WAYS IN    <command> -?      most programs answer with a syntax line    help <topic>      the OS-9 HELP utility, from /dd/SYS/HELP:                          export HELPDIR=/dd/SYS/HELP     (bash)                          setenv HELPDIR /dd/SYS/HELP     (the OS-9 shell)                      HELP and helpindex are (c) 1989 Lukas Zeller, the                      author of os9exec; his conditions ask that help.hlp                      and helpindex ship with it, and they do (DOC/help).                      A new topic: write <name>.hlp, then                          chd /dd/SYS/HELP; helpindex <name>.hlp    nroff -man <page> by hand.  Set TMACDIR=/dd/LIB first, or nroff says                      `unable to open macro file /tmac.an'.  The -man                      macros in /dd/LIB came with the nroff source.WHICH PROGRAM IS WHICH    DOC/STATUS         works / needs cio / broken -- start here    DOC/INDEX          one line saying what every program IS    DOC/ORIGINS        one line saying where every program CAME FROM    DOC/NEEDCIO-INDEX  the cio-requiring set, and where to get cio    DOC/EFFO-INFO      the EFFO authors' own descriptions AND licence                       conditions -- some programs here say 'no military use'    SOURCES.txt        licence, build method, and what was left out and why